GTOpt @VERSION@ - binary release for Linux x86_64
==================================================

GTOpt (Generation, Transmission and storage Optimization) builds sparse
LP/MIP formulations of multi-stage power systems (expansion planning,
hydrothermal scheduling with SDDP, unit commitment, economic dispatch)
and solves them with pluggable solver backends.

Source revision: @GIT_REVISION@
Project page:    https://github.com/gtopt-community/gtopt
Documentation:   https://github.com/gtopt-community/gtopt/tree/v@VERSION@/docs


Requirements
------------

* Linux x86_64 with glibc >= @GLIBC@ and libstdc++ providing
  GLIBCXX_@GLIBCXX@.  Tested on Ubuntu 24.04 LTS and
  newer; Debian 13 and other distributions with the same or newer glibc
  and GCC runtime should work.  Ubuntu 22.04 and older are NOT supported
  by this binary (build from source instead, see BUILDING.md).
* Apache Arrow/Parquet, HiGHS, COIN-OR CBC/CLP, spdlog, jemalloc and
  their dependencies are bundled in lib/.  The only system libraries
  used are glibc (libc, libm, ...), libstdc++6, libgcc-s1 and OpenSSL 3
  (libssl.so.3), which every supported system has installed.  On a
  minimal container image install them with:
      apt-get install libstdc++6 libgcc-s1 libssl3t64   # Ubuntu 24.04+, Debian 13


Install
-------

    tar --zstd -xf gtopt-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64.tar.zst   # or: tar -xzf ...tar.gz
    sudo mv gtopt-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64 /opt/gtopt-@VERSION@
    sudo ln -sf /opt/gtopt-@VERSION@/bin/gtopt /usr/local/bin/gtopt

Or without root:

    mkdir -p ~/.local/opt ~/.local/bin
    tar --zstd -xf gtopt-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64.tar.zst -C ~/.local/opt
    ln -sf ~/.local/opt/gtopt-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64/bin/gtopt ~/.local/bin/gtopt

The tree is relocatable: bin/gtopt finds its libraries in ../lib and its
solver plugins in ../lib/gtopt/plugins wherever the directory is placed.
Keep the layout intact (do not copy bin/gtopt alone).

Verify the download first:

    sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS --ignore-missing


Run
---

    gtopt --version
    gtopt --solvers              # lists the available LP/MIP backends

    cp -r share/gtopt/examples/c0 /tmp/c0 && cd /tmp/c0
    gtopt system_c0.json --solver highs --set output_directory=out
    cat out/solution.csv         # status "optimal", obj_value ~ 23163.42

See docs/usage.md in the source tree for all options.


Solvers
-------

Included (open source):  HiGHS (libgtopt_solver_highs.so) and COIN-OR
CLP/CBC (libgtopt_solver_osi.so).  The default backend is chosen
automatically; select one with `--solver highs|clp|cbc`.

Commercial solvers (CPLEX, Gurobi, MindOpt) and the GPU solver cuOpt are
NOT included.  Their plugins must be built from source against your own
licensed installation (see BUILDING.md) and placed in
lib/gtopt/plugins/, or in a directory named by $GTOPT_PLUGIN_DIR.


Python tools
------------

The converters and utilities (plp2gtopt, plexos2gtopt, pp2gtopt,
gtopt_diagram, run_gtopt, ...) are released as the `gtopt-scripts`
wheel attached to the same GitHub Release:

    python3 -m venv ~/.local/share/gtopt/venv
    ~/.local/share/gtopt/venv/bin/pip install gtopt_scripts-@VERSION@-py3-none-any.whl


Debugging
---------

bin/gtopt and the plugins are stripped.  Their debug information (line
tables) is in gtopt-@VERSION@-linux-x86_64-debug.tar.zst; extract it on
top of this directory and gdb picks it up through .gnu_debuglink.


